      <title>Utah monument could be the latest target of a law to undo public lands decisions</title>
      <link>https://www.kunr.org/2026-03-03/utah-monument-could-be-the-latest-target-of-a-law-to-undo-public-lands-decisions</link>
      <description>Republican lawmakers are increasingly turning to the Congressional Review Act to overturn federal agency decisions, including public lands management plans in Montana and Wyoming last year. But it has never before been used to target a national monument.</description>
